DECISIONS (stated assumptions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. OUTPUT PATH NORMALIZED. The generator template named
   apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**, but that path is NOT a source root in
   apps/apple/project.yml (sources: Sources, TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets,
   TeslaSync/feature-views, Localization) NOR in .swiftlint.yml `included`. A file
   there would neither compile into the app targets nor be linted. The repo's real
   compiled feature root is Sources/Features/<Domain>/ (Sources/Features/Dashboard/
   already exists). The page was therefore placed at
   apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/ so it actually builds + lints. Per
   p4-apple/README binding rule 1 the only hard constraint is apps/apple/**.
2. FIRST-CLASS ROUTE. The shell route host (Sources/App/RouteHostRegistry.swift)
   is keyed by AppRoute, so a first-class, deep-linkable, testable destination
   (matching web's first-class /tesla-region page) requires an AppRoute case.
   Added .teslaRegion. AppRouteParser resolves /tesla-region automatically by
   pathSegment (no parser edit needed). Group: web's "Integrations" sidebar group
   has no Apple peer; .account (Settings/Onboarding) is the closest semantic
   bucket and the underlying surface is features/settings/components/RegionSettings.
3. DEFERRED LIVE SOURCE. The embedded RegionSettings surface (P4 feature view 0211,
   already in-repo) binds through RegionSettingsModel ← RegionSettingsSource. The
   production live source (shared-core useTeslaUserRegion()) is wired centrally in
   AppContainer.bootstrap(baseURL:), which is deferred app-wide (see AppContainer.swift;
   precedent: UnavailableVehicleCommanding in TeslaSyncApp). The composition root
   therefore builds the child model on InMemoryRegionSettingsSource() — the surface
   shows its initial loading state until that wiring lands. The page is a pure
   function of its injected model; no networking added here. This is the page-level
   parity unit (2 strings); the RegionSettings data-binding is a separate unit (0211).

